{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782177245,"nonce":"LQv1WTfDGe/6FpO8h0p+4YrqmkA=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGXC_jg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/311","origin":"github"},"title":"RCA: survey pattern stops short → hover, then erratic following on drawn trackline (2026-06-22 Massabesic)","message":"RCA follow-up from the 2026-06-22 Lake Massabesic survey deployment ([#309](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/309)). Two related path-following anomalies occurred in one incident around **14:37 EDT**.\n\n## Symptoms (operator-corrected timeline)\n\n1. The autonomous **survey pattern stopped a few tracklines short** of completing and the boat went into a **hover**.\n2. The hover prompted the operators to **draw a new (recovery) trackline**.\n3. The boat followed the drawn trackline OK, then **erratic path-following began a few segments in** (\"Bizzy is going crazy\"). It was mitigated by reverting `controller_server` `FollowPath.lookahead_time` 3.0 → 0.0; controller_server stayed [active] across the revert.\n\nThe erratic onset was well into the drawn trackline, **not** at the hover transition — so these read as two distinct phenomena worth separating in analysis.\n\n## Hypotheses\n\n- **(a) Stop-short → hover** — operator hypothesis: the next survey start point may have been **outside the local_costmap**, so the planner could not plan to it. Check `local_costmap` size/bounds vs the survey-pattern segment spacing; if start points can fall outside the rolling window, planning fails and the boat holds. Possible fixes: larger local costmap, or a global-planner fallback when the target is beyond the local window.\n- **(b) Erratic following** — `lookahead_time = 3.0` (velocity × 3 s lookahead) is **one unconfirmed hypothesis** among several; the temporal correlation is suggestive but the operator is not sure it was causal. Could also be path geometry of the hand-drawn trackline, controller tuning, or interaction with the costmap state after the hover.\n\n## Evidence / where to look\n\n- Bag (offline read): `gabby/logs/bizzyboat/2026-06-22T13-22-29+00-00` — focus the **14:37 EDT** window. Topics of interest: `/bizzy/odom`, `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos`, `/bizzy/local_costmap/costmap`, controller/planner state, and the FollowPath params.\n- Deployment GPS context (for time alignment): cast-off 09:58, dock return 16:30 EDT.\n- Note: ballast was removed 2026-06-19, so handling dynamics differ from earlier ballasted runs (unlikely to cause this, but relevant if controller behavior is in question).\n\n## Out of scope here\n\nThe CA/controller tunes field-validated this day (CA box half-widths, `obstacle_avoidance_weight` 1.0) are intentional and being landed via the wrap-up PR; not part of this RCA.\n\nPart of the #309 deployment follow-up.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}